# The public C ABI. Every identifier here follows C convention (kb_snake_case
# types/functions, KB_UPPER enum constants), which the root config's C++ naming
# rules (CamelCase enums, k-prefixed constants) would flag wholesale. The root
# .clang-tidy already declares this surface out of scope in prose; this makes it
# so. Everything else in the root config still applies via InheritParentConfig.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -readability-identifier-naming
